hermes-office local patch — NOT an upstream pull request.

Target: clawmem@0.43.5, applied against the installed npm package root
(/usr/local/lib/node_modules/clawmem), AFTER 036, 040, 041, 042 and 043.

Why: patch 042 taught the runtime that `off` is a legal reasoning_effort, but the
doctor's endpoint probe was left behind. `LlamaCpp.probeChatCompletionsShape()`
(llm.ts) sends a fixed body — model / one user message / max_tokens: 8 /
temperature: 0 — and never sends reasoning_effort. Against a reasoning model that
is 8 tokens of reasoning_content and nothing else:

  no reasoning_effort   content=None    reasoning_tokens=8   finish_reason=length
  reasoning_effort=off  content="OK"    reasoning_tokens=0

The shape check then reports `choices[0].message.content is not a string`, and
`clawmem doctor` prints:

  ✗ LLM endpoint: ... answered 200 but the body is not a chat-completions
    response (choices[0].message.content is not a string) — wrong service on
    the port?

for an endpoint that is serving that very model correctly. Reproduced 3/3 against
the live gateway while the runtime path (generate() -> buildRemoteLlmRequest(),
which does send the effort) answered a normal JSON extraction in 1196 ms. A
diagnostic that cries wolf on the deployment it is meant to certify is worse than
no diagnostic: it is the only signal that the shared LLM lane — observer,
decision extractor, A-MEM, handoff — is alive, and it now fails for every
reasoning model on every gateway.

What:
  llm.ts      probeChatCompletionsShape() takes an optional reasoningEffort and
              puts it on the wire only when set (absent config keeps the body
              byte-identical to stock). Its shape-failure detail now carries
              finish_reason and reasoning_tokens, so a truncated-but-real reply
              reads as `(finish_reason=length, reasoning_tokens=8)` instead of
              accusing the port of running the wrong service.
  clawmem.ts  the doctor call site passes
              normalizeRemoteLlmReasoningEffort(CLAWMEM_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT),
              the same normalizer the request builders use, so the probe and the
              runtime cannot drift apart again.

Deliberately NOT changed: max_tokens stays 8 and a non-string content still
fails the probe. Raising the budget would make a thinking model pass by luck
(deepseek spends 500+ tokens reasoning), and accepting content:null would delete
the check that catches a genuinely wrong service on the port. The fix is to send
the policy, not to weaken the assertion.

Retire together with 042 if upstream probes with the configured effort itself.

